# Moltology Project Intelligence

Cross-reference: [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) for full system rules.

## Verification priority (default)

Use headless terminal checks only. Never default to browser or GUI verification.

- **Single file**: `npx vitest run path/to/file.test.ts` or `npm run test:file -- path/to/file.test.ts` (~0.4s)
- **Typecheck**: `npm run typecheck` for TS validation without a production build
- **Follow AGENTS.md tiers**:
  - **Tier 1** (scoped/feature): touched file(s) or `npm run test:changed` + `npm run typecheck`
  - **Tier 2** (lib/db/auth/ingest): `npm run test:core` (~9s) or `npm run test:scripts`
  - **Tier 3** (major refactor/release): `npm run test` + `npm run build` only

## Verification commands

| Command | Scope | Approx. cost |
|---------|-------|--------------|
| `npx vitest run src/lib/foo.test.ts` | Single file | ~0.4s |
| `npm run test:changed` | Git-changed tests | varies |
| `npm run test:core` | `src/lib` + `src/db` | 51 files, ~9s |
| `npm run test:ui` | components, routes, hooks | ~86 files |
| `npm run test:scripts` | `scripts/` | ~10 files |
| `npm run test` | Full suite | 147 files, ~21s |
| `npm run typecheck` | TS only | fast |
| `npm run build` | Production bundle | heavy — Tier 3 only |

Vitest runs headless in jsdom ([vite.config.ts](vite.config.ts)); TanStack Start/Nitro plugins are disabled during tests.

## Forbidden unless user explicitly asks

- Browser MCP automation (`browser_navigate`, screenshot loops, visual QA)
- Starting `npm run dev` or `npm run preview` for verification
- Heavy GUI/Chrome pipelines: `mockups:capture`, `composite:render`, `post:create`, video/reel scripts
- Full suite (`npm run test`) or `npm run build` for localized edits
- Re-running `npm install` when `node_modules` exists and lockfile is unchanged

## Allowed when user requests

- Visual QA, mockup capture, or "check in browser"
- Skill-driven pipelines (mockup-capture, instagram-post-creator, etc.)

## Dependency caching (Cloud Agents)

Cloud Builds run `install` in [.cursor/environment.json](.cursor/environment.json) and persist `node_modules`. No dev server auto-starts — agents must not boot `npm run dev` unless the user asks.

- Skip `npm install` unless `package.json` / `package-lock.json` changed or install errors occur
- Do not delete `node_modules`
- Ensure Cloud Agent Builds are enabled in the Cursor dashboard
